// The borer steers like a worm, in every direction. Ridden from a chamber into solid granite, the walking keys point
// the way: right, then down (its head swings round in a curve, not snapping), then down and right together (a
// diagonal), then up (it turns back the short way, through east, and bores up), then left: the head goes where it is
// pointed, at granite speed all the way, cutting its round tunnel along the curve.
map
